": \"The instrumentation module is built against MongoDB Java driver 3.1 APIs such as com.mongodb.event.CommandListener and MongoClientOptions, but its published POM/Gradle metadata does not bring the driver transitively.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n          \"image\": \"mongo:4.2\",\n          \"slug\": \"mongo\",\n          \"reason\": \"The upstream OpenTelemetry Mongo 3.1 instrumentation tests exercise real MongoClient command listener callbacks against a MongoDB container, and documentation shows the listener attached to a client connecting to a MongoDB endpoint.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"agent_guidance\": \"Use the MongoDB 3.x client API: build MongoClientOptions, add MongoTelemetry.create(...).createCommandListener(), and point the client at the prepared test server host/port. For focused unit coverage without relying on every database operation, CommandStartedEvent/CommandSucceededEvent/CommandFailedEvent can also be constructed directly to exercise the listener path. Only set -Dotel.semconv-stability.opt-in=database if the tests intentionally assert the stable database semantic-convention attributes.\",\n      \"risks\": [\n        \"The upstream tests use an older MongoDB server tag; local Docker/native-image verification remains authoritative for image availability and vulnerability policy.\",\n        \"Using a newer MongoDB driver artifact instead of the 3.1-era driver may shift APIs and instrumentation behavior away from the module's minimum supported surface.\"\n      ],\n      \"applied_setup\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n          \"coordinate\": \"org.mongodb:mongo-java-driver:3.1.0\",\n          \"result\": \"applied\",\n          \"target\": \"tests/src/io.opentelemetry.instrumentation/opentelemetry-mongo-3.1/2.28.1-alpha/build.gradle\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n          \"image\": \"mongo:4.2\",\n          \"slug\": \"mongo\",\n          \"r